Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(food):=20whole=20days=20only=20in=20every?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20average;=20=C2=ABTu=20gasto=20real=C2=BB=20with=20Hall's=20k?=
 =?UTF-8?q?cal=20per=20kg=20and=20the=20current=20streak?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A logged day is complete when it has a dinner or reaches 75 % of the median of the logged days in the 28
before it (FoodDays.isComplete / completeDays). Partly logged days stay on the charts and leave the
history's averages and average balance, the per-meal averages, the weekly points (whose burn now averages
the same complete days, B17), «Tu gasto real», the coach's FOOD LOG average and ENERGY BALANCE, and are
marked in the week's prompt. "Semana" is the seven days before today plus today, as the coach's (B5).
The burn is plotted on logged days only: without meals the model has no digestion term, so an unlogged
day would draw a dip that is only a missing log.

«Tu gasto real»: the engine's slope re-centred on Hall 2008's kcal per kg (p = 10.4 / (10.4 + fat mass),
9 400·(1 − p) + 1 800·p; 0.25 without a scale), weigh-ins from three days before the current logging
streak (B19), compared with the model's total over the same complete days, on the logical "today".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
